  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Seven Rocks. Enforce single-spinner rules, legal end matching, pass when blocked, and immediate score updates from open-end totals.',
    Player: 'In Seven Rocks, prioritize legal plays that produce immediate multiple-of-five end totals while preserving good follow-ups for your partner.',
    objective: 'Be the first partnership to reach 250 points by making the open ends of the cross-shaped layout total a multiple of five when possible and by minimizing hand-end pip penalties.',
    gameplay: "Lead any tile. Players in turn must match an open end; if no match is possible they pass. The first double played is the only spinner and creates the cross-style expansion pattern. After each play, score immediately if exposed ends total 5, 10, 15, 20, 25 or 30. A hand ends when someone dominoes or all players are blocked. Then each player's remaining pips are rounded to nearest five and subtracted from that player's score.",
    keyRules: [
      'Only the first double is a spinner.',
      'No boneyard exists in Seven Rocks.',
      'Passing is required when no legal tile can be played.',
      'If the previous hand was blocked, the next opening lead is determined by lot.',
    ],
